# tighConaillRescue -- the champion, half-drowned, in Conall's cabin
#
# Plays BEFORE the curtain (tighConaill.dlg), in four parts (tighConaill.js, _dream):
#   node 0 -- in the dark: black screen, soft rain, the drowning, "Lie still."   (the eyes then open)
#   node 1 -- half-woken: "where is this place", "I am Conall"
#   node 2 -- "the mark of a student of Dún Scáthach. It is thine."              (the brooch is thrown when this card closes)
#   node 3 -- "I bring no cattle" ... "the path of the blade"
# Nodes 0, 1 and 3 have no card of their own, only the exchange. Every node closes the
# conversation; the scene plays them with _talk(1, 0) ... _talk(1, 3).
#
# IRISH IS A FIRST DRAFT -- check before shipping.

@file skye/tighConaill
@encounter 1


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — in the dark

> Drowning!
% Ag bá!
> The black water has me,
% Tá mé i ngreim ag an uisce dubh,
> It fills my throat.
% líonann sé mo scornach.

< Lie still.
% Bí socair.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — half-woken

> I was drowning. I was surely drowning.
% Bhí mé báite. Bhí mé báite gan amhras.

< Thou art weary, nothing more.
% Níl ort ach tuirse.

> Where is this place?
% Cá bhfuil mé anois?

< Thou art my guest. I am Conall.
% Mo aoi thú. Conall is ainm dom.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2 — the mark
And this is the mark of a student of Dún Scáthach. It is thine.
% Chaitheann dhaltaí Dhún Scáthach iad seo. Is leatsa é.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 3 — the path of the blade

> I bring no cattle, no fine tribute of silver.
% Níor thugas liom eallach, ná tiarnas breá airgid.

< Ease now thy troubled mind
% Bí socair
< Thou hast made thy case already upon the shore, senseless and half-drowned,
% Rinne tú do chás cheana féin nuair a bhain tú amach an trá, gan aithne, leathbáite,
< with the sea still running from thee.
% agus an fharraige fós ag sileadh uait.
< Take thy rest,
% Lig do scíth,
< Then shall I set thee on the path of the blade,
% Ansin cuirfidh mé ar bhóthar an chlaímh thú,
< Is that not why all Gaelic Chieftains come to Skye?
% Nach é sin a tógann na Taoisigh Gaelach ar fad go Cheo?
